Subject: [PATCH] A Claude account Anthropic answers authentication_failed is
 followed by the subscription's other accounts in the same re

## What happens

When Anthropic refuses a Claude subscription account's sign-in on a try,
Claude Code reports the error kind `authentication_failed`, and the bridge
carries it as the try's `ErrType`. `serve`'s `failAuth` branch
(internal/gateway/gateway.go) marks the account lapsed and sends the same
request to the subscription's next account. Nothing handles
`authentication_failed` itself.

## Why it matters

A revoked OAuth token is how a banned account answers. Whatever Anthropic
acted on (the request's content, the user) goes with the request to every
account it reaches next. In one server's usage export, a banned account
failed with authentication_failed at 14:24:26. The same session was on
another account in the same minute, and that account was banned 19 minutes
later. Two more accounts went the same way.

magpie already walls a provider off for the rest of a request when its
vendor's risk control restricts an account (`riskRefused`, for WorkBuddy and
ZCode). Claude has no such wall.

## Reproduction (main 71fbb33a)

Two tests in internal/gateway/claude_auth_wall_test.go, with a fake Claude
Code whose first account answers as Claude Code does for a revoked token:

```
{"type":"assistant","message":{...,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Failed to authenticate: OAuth token revoked. ..."}]},"error":"authentication_failed"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":true,"api_error_status":403,"result":"Failed to authenticate: OAuth token revoked. ..."}
```

```
go test -count=1 -run 'TestClaudeAuthFailed' -v ./internal/gateway

--- FAIL: TestClaudeAuthFailedWallsTheOtherAccounts
    .../auth/stream=true:  claude_auth_wall_test.go:48: the spare was asked after authentication_failed: 200 runs "own,tok-spare"
    .../auth/stream=false: claude_auth_wall_test.go:48: the spare was asked after authentication_failed: 200 runs "own,tok-spare"
    (the overloaded cases pass: a 529 still goes on to the spare)
--- FAIL: TestClaudeAuthFailedGroupGoesToItsOtherProvider
    claude_auth_wall_test.go:73: 200 ...; the other provider asked 0 times; Claude runs "own,tok-spare"
```

## The fix

The patch below / linked branch (3 files, +134):

- `claudeAuthWalled(c, errType)` (fallback.go): a Claude subscription
  account whose try's ErrType is `authentication_failed`.
- In `serve`, before the `failAuth` hand-on, a walled try drops the
  provider's other accounts from the request's candidates, from `busyNow`
  and from `small`/`smallW` (`elsewhere`, `elsewhereWeighed`), as
  `riskRefused` does. Another provider in a group is still asked. The
  account is still marked lapsed by the existing branch, and nothing else is
  held.

Claude Code also reports an ordinary refused sign-in ("Please run /login",
any other 401/403 of Anthropic's API) as authentication_failed. So an
expired sign-in also stops that one request from going on to the
subscription's other accounts. Other requests are not affected.

Not in the patch: a docs line in docs/subsystems/gateway-routing.md beside
the `riskRefused` wall.

## Possible follow-up (not in this issue)

Holding the caller or the account for a while after authentication_failed
(for example 12 hours), until the user acts, would be new policy and UI.
It isn't needed to fix the hand-on above and can be proposed separately.

Run at this tree (base origin/main 2219fdd4, macOS arm64, go1.26.8):
- go test -count=1 -run 'ClaudeAuthFailed|Claude|Fallback|Wall' ./internal/gateway: ok (87s)
- gofmt -l internal: clean; GOOS=windows go vet on the changed packages: ok.
Not run: the full suite.

